BudPilot License
Version 1.0, 22 November 2026

Copyright (c) 2026 wahidalways. All rights reserved.

BudPilot is free for everyone to use. This license explains what you may do
with BudPilot, what needs permission first, and the rules that protect you
and the author. It is written in plain English on purpose.


1. Words used in this license

"BudPilot" means the BudPilot app and everything in this repository
(https://github.com/wahidalways/BudPilot): its source code, design, text,
graphics, name and icons.

"The author" means wahidalways, who owns BudPilot.

"You" means anyone who gets, uses or reads BudPilot, and any company or
group you act for.

"An official build" means an APK, EXE or other installer published on this
repository's Releases page (https://github.com/wahidalways/BudPilot/releases).

"A changed version" means anything made by changing, adding to, removing
from, translating or repackaging BudPilot, other than the build settings
allowed in section 2.4.

"Written permission" means a message from the author that clearly gives
permission, such as a reply from the wahidalways account on GitHub.
Permission covers only what it says.


2. What you may do, for free

2.1 Use. Install and use BudPilot on any number of devices, for any
    purpose. This includes businesses, schools and other organizations, and
    their work devices.

2.2 Share person to person. Give an official build, unchanged and for free,
    directly to people you know, for example by sending them the file.

2.3 Read and learn. Read the source code to learn how BudPilot works.

2.4 Build and change it for yourself. Build BudPilot from this source code,
    and change it, for your own private use. Changing only build settings,
    such as the Expo account, is fine. Keep changed code private: on your
    own devices or in a private repository.

2.5 Talk about BudPilot. Use the BudPilot name and icon to refer to
    BudPilot, for example in reviews, articles, videos, tutorials and links
    to the official page, as long as you do not suggest that the author
    made, approved or supports your work.


3. What needs written permission first

Unless the author gives you written permission, you may not:

3.1 Share or publish a changed version of BudPilot in any form. This
    includes a public fork with changes and a build made from changed code.

3.2 Upload or offer BudPilot, even unchanged, on any website, app store,
    file-sharing service or other public place, other than this repository.

3.3 Sell BudPilot, charge money for it or for access to it, add ads to it,
    collect payments through it, or include it in anything you sell, such
    as earbuds or phones sold with BudPilot.

3.4 Copy any part of BudPilot's code, design, text or graphics into another
    app, website or project.

3.5 Use the BudPilot name or icon for another app or product, for a changed
    version, or in any way that could make people think something is
    official BudPilot.

3.6 Use BudPilot's code, design or other content to train, fine-tune or
    test an AI or machine-learning model, or to build a dataset for one.

3.7 Remove or change this license, or the copyright notice above, in any
    copy of BudPilot's source code.


4. Asking for permission

To ask, open an issue at https://github.com/wahidalways/BudPilot/issues and
explain what you want to do. The author may say yes, say no, or set
conditions such as credit or payment. No answer means no permission.


5. Bug reports, ideas and outside code

Bug reports, ideas and requests for new earbuds are welcome as GitHub
issues. If you share an idea or other feedback, the author may use it
freely, without owing you anything. BudPilot does not take outside code, so
pull requests may be closed without review.


6. GitHub

GitHub's terms let anyone view and fork this repository on GitHub, and this
license does not take that away. A fork may be kept as it is or for your own
use, but publishing changes in it, or releasing builds from it, is covered
by section 3.


7. Open-source parts and other people's names

BudPilot is built with open-source libraries, such as React Native and
Expo. Each library keeps its own license, and that license, not this one,
covers the library. This license gives you no rights in those libraries
beyond what their own licenses give.

BudPilot is not made, approved or supported by any earbud maker or chip
maker. Their names appear only to say which devices BudPilot works with,
and they belong to their owners.


8. Fair use

Nothing in this license limits what the law already lets you do without
permission, such as fair use or fair dealing. For example, you may quote a
short part of the code in a review or a lesson.


9. No warranty

BudPilot is provided "as is" and "as available", without any warranty,
express or implied. This includes any warranty that it is fit for a
particular purpose, works without errors, or works with your earbuds.
BudPilot sends commands to your earbuds over Bluetooth. You use it at your
own risk.


10. Limit of liability

As far as the law allows, the author is not liable for any loss or damage
that comes from using BudPilot, or from not being able to use it. This
includes harm to earbuds or other devices, lost data and lost profits,
whatever the legal reason for the claim. Some places do not allow these
limits, so they apply only as far as the law where you live allows.


11. When your rights end

If you break this license, your rights under it end automatically. If it is
the first time, and you fully stop within 30 days after the author tells you
about it, your rights come back as if they had never ended. Sections 9, 10,
12 and 14 still apply after your rights end.


12. Law and courts

This license is governed by the laws of Bangladesh, and the courts of
Bangladesh decide any dispute about it, except where the law where you live
gives you, as a consumer, the right to use your own courts.


13. New versions of this license

The author may publish new versions of this license for future releases of
BudPilot. Each release is covered by the license in this repository when
that release came out. A new version never takes away rights you already
had for an older release.


14. Other terms

This license, together with any written permission from the author, is the
whole agreement about BudPilot. If a court finds part of it unenforceable,
the rest stays in force, and that part applies as far as it can. If the
author does not act on a breach right away, the author can still act on it
later. All rights not given in this license are kept by the author.
